## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical knowledge of enforcing strict multi-tenant isolation, combining API gateway ABAC, envelope encryption, tenancy separation in data stores, and incident response readiness in a real-world, globally distributed ride-hailing context.

## Key Concepts

- ABAC policies per tenant at API gateway
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant keys (KMS)
- Service mesh mTLS and SPIRE identities
- Per-tenant data stores and RLS
- IR playbooks with cross-region logs and forensics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example access check
function authorize(user, resource) {
  if (user.tenant_id !== resource.tenant_id) {
    throw new Error('tenant_mismatch');
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without downtime?
- What metrics define measurable success criteria for this plan?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical application of confidential computing to multi-tenant isolation in real-time ML workloads, beyond token-based controls.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (TDX/Nitro/SEV)
- Per-tenant attested enclaves and key management
- Envelope encryption of in-flight data and outputs
- Attestation-based admission control at API gateway
- IR playbook with measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-spec showing attestation flow
function attestedInference(req, enclave) {
  if (!enclave.attest(req.tenant)) throw new Error('Untrusted tenant');
  const input = enclave.declassify(req.input, req.tenant);
  const out = enclave.infer(input);
  return enclave.envelope(out, req.tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without service downtime?
- How would you detect and respond to a compromised enclave?
